        "thought_text": "Thought-2: The error in the previous implementation was that it didn't correctly handle the case where no adjustment is needed (i.e., when all hills are already suitable for construction). The binary search was not properly initialized to account for this scenario, leading to incorrect results in some cases. To fix this, we need to modify our approach to handle this edge case more effectively. Specifically, we should first check if any adjustments are needed at all, and if not, we should return 0 for all k values. This will ensure that we correctly handle cases where the initial sequence is already suitable for construction.",
